.Sh NAME
.Nm wattle-check
.Nd compile a script without running it
.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm "wattle check"
.Oo
.Ar options
.Oc
.Oo
.Ar script
.Oc
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm "wattle check"
compiles
.Ar script
without running it and reports compilation errors.
If no script is specified,
the command reads source from standard input.
.Ic c
is a synonym for
.Cm check .
.Pp
By default,
the command reports all errors and exits with status 0.
With
.Fl b ,
it stops at the first error and exits with status 1.
.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Fl e ,
.Fl "-lint-error"
.Ar level
.Xc
Set the lint level at which a message stops compilation with
an error.
.Ar level
is one of
.Ql "none" ,
.Ql "relaxed" ,
.Ql "normal" ,
.Ql "strict"
or
.Ql "all" ,
written without a leading colon.
These names correspond to the numeric levels 0,
1,
2,
3 and infinity.
A numeric level can also be given directly.
A message is reported when its level is at most
.Ar level .
As a result,
.Ql "none"
reports no messages and
.Ql "all"
reports every message.
The default is
.Ql "none" .
.It Xo
.Fl w ,
.Fl "-lint-warn"
.Ar level
.Xc
Set the lint level at which a message is printed as a warning.
.Ar level
takes the same values as for
.Fl e .
The default is
.Ql "normal" .
.It Xo
.Fl b ,
.Fl "-bail"
.Xc
Stop at the first error in the source and exit with status 1.
.El
.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Check a script for compile errors without running it,
stopping at the first:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ wattle check --bail hello\&.wattle
.Ed
.
